		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4732&amp;p=34992#p34992"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>This most recent update (beta, I guess?) disabled the GPS on my MD-UV380.  I purchased this radio a year ago and installed OpenGD77 and have had no issues with the firmware, nor any issues with GPS.  After installing this particular update, the only "option" for GPS under General Options is "None".  (cue "sad trombone")<br><br>I've tried addressing the issue by applying older firmware, to no avail.  Not really sure what else to try or do.  Any thoughts?</div></blockquote>Try resetting the settings. <br><br>If that doesn't work,  Try going back to a much older version e.g. the stable release from December 2023, as that would still have GPS support<br><br>If that still doesn't work, then perhaps you have an intermittent fault with the GPS hardware<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Sat Jan 04, 2025 10:27 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
